At the risk of teaching grandma to suck eggs:
OK. Be advised that the build of Qt takes several hours (on a G4 
400), and in my experience fails when it looks in /usr/lib/ for a 
library when building 'uic', when it should be looking in 
$QTDIR/lib. If you watch $QTDIR/lib/ for new libraries during the 
build and make symlinks in /usr/lib/ as they appear, then it all 
works smoothly. Alternatively make those symlinks when the build 
falls over.
[Note: I don't use fink, which may impact this...]

Also, the Qt/Mac Free distrib doesn't include the multi-threading 
libraries, so you'll be moving just libqt.<version>.dylib. [I used 
the 3.2.3 lib, but have successfully tested a late December 3.3.0b1 
snapshot too]

